    not_duplicate_of: []  # e4aa
    pr_ref:  # e4aa
    description: "CARRIER — DO NOT WORK THIS ITEM DIRECTLY. It is the durable representation of an owner deferral,\nnot a task. Its only job is to hold INV-zogud-vanov-badoh-gogap-dizud-hogab-gokok-dulik out of the\nwork queue until the taint / DDG / dataflow / CFG / io-boundaries area is straightened out.\n\nTHE DEFERRAL: owner ruling 2026-08-05 — \"hold off on INV-zogud until we get this taint/DDG/data\nflow/CFG/io boundaries stuff straightened out.\" Recorded in full on INV-zogud itself.\n\nWHY A CARRIER AND NOT PROSE: the PREVIOUS deferral of INV-zogud expired SILENTLY when its stated\nrationale (the nine-phase taint campaign) ended, and a human had to notice twice. Before this item\nexisted the new deferral lived only in a discussion entry, while INV-zogud sat at rank 84 of 182 in\nscripts/tracker ready — i.e. the hold was asserted in prose and contradicted by the queue.\n\nMECHANISM (verified, not assumed): store.py:2550-2556 builds blocked_ids from the isbefore targets\nof every item whose status is NOT in resolved_statuses, and ready() drops those targets. Config\nresolved_statuses = [done, wont_do, deleted, satisfied, ...]; blocking_statuses = [todo_hard,\ntodo_soft, violated, pending_validation, in_progress]. Note needs_human_review is in NEITHER, so a\ncarrier parked there still blocks its target while itself vanishing from ready. Positive control\nrecorded above; the post-condition is that INV-zogud no longer appears in ready.\n\nRESOLVING THIS ITEM RELEASES THE MYPY CAMPAIGN. Do not resolve it because it looks stale, because\nnothing has moved, or because a session wants INV-zogud back. Inactivity is not discharge.\n\nWHAT THE OWNER HAS AND HAS NOT DECIDED (as of 2026-08-05):\n  DECIDED — the deferral itself; and that only this carrier edge is built now (\"Part C only for\n    now\"). A machine-witnessed build gate and a decision gate were designed, adversarially\n    reviewed, and DEFERRED — see below.\n  NOT DECIDED — what \"straightened out\" means. There is no ratified exit condition. Filling that\n    in is the first thing anyone picking this up should ask about.\n\nWHY THE BUILD GATE WAS DEFERRED (owner reasoning, and it generalizes): the mechanism that produces\nthis area's numbers is itself in flux, so pinning a measured vector now would seed an INVERTED\nbaseline. Concretely: fixing WI-votom-tuvik-bikof-kazuh-vonuv-mimag-jajoj-torig UN-suppresses real\nleaks and RAISES the unsanitized-flow count, so a shrink-only ceiling on that quantity would fail\non the correctness fix and read a suppression regression as progress. Same argument parked the\nself-audit adjudication — see WI-vanun-mofih-zikot-hutos-dosub-buroz-fumas-fufog.\n\nTHE AREA, AS MAPPED 2026-08-05 (full map: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-map-08052026.md;\n53 keyword-and-tag candidates screened → 20 IN, 12 ADJACENT, 21 OUT):\n  One production entry point (cmd_verify_claims → _build_ddg_for_verify_claims → build_repo_ddg)\n  and one user-visible exit (verify-claims). Nothing else in the product runs a CFG. 10,171 lines\n  of core Python + 1,205 lines of def/use extractors + 4,992 lines of YAML across 46 catalogs.\n\nBLOCKING STRUCTURE — only INV-lupav has no external blocker:\n  INV-lupav-bigak-zirob-gofun-sopod-sirij-panal-dinav (P0) → WI-joluk + WI-votom, both buildable\n  INV-sadah-gifob-nujob-tovan-kinos-vovuk-kupon-mibuj (P1) → S2 via WI-kabif → prereq 7 = INV-busis\n  INV-busis-povul-butun-kosut-tozik-jarok-vokaz-vomur (P1) → an ADR-0017 section 7a/7b owner ruling\n  INV-karud-nozoh-zolup-bopob-jukus-rujus-rorol-kakaj (P2, 5 clauses, 2 satisfied) → a2 inherits\n    INV-busis entire; (a1) has no open item named as its vehicle; (b) is unexerciseable through the\n    shipped python catalog until WI-makij lands\n\nTHE TWO UNMEASURED NUMBERS THAT PRICE THE RULING (both ruling-independent, both in flight):\n  1. The split of INV-busis clause B1b's 86 genuine-non-call blockers into field-write /\n     container-subscript / capture-mediated-closure. This matters because ADR-0017 section 7a\n     INCLUDES the first two (\"if x is tainted then x.field, x.method() and x[key] inherit x\n     taint\"; \"if obj.field = tainted_value then obj.field is tainted\") — they are declared in\n     scope and simply unbuilt (is_field_tainted at taint.py:1843 has zero production callers).\n     Only capture-mediated closure taint sits behind the section 7b line. So the ruling is\n     narrower than the campaign framing assumed.\n  2. How many of those escape sites carry a usable access_mode stamp. ADR-0038 states in four\n     places that access_mode is a designed input to taint propagation, with a recorded ordering\n     constraint (\"access_mode rebuild — before taint work\") that was violated: ruling 1 is PARTIAL\n     (the line-granular classifier it was to replace still runs at dataflow.py:546-563, consumed\n     at :595) and ruling 5 is ABSENT (grep ast_name_read spec_validator.py → 0 hits). Caveat: the\n     join is nontrivial (access_mode is per-edge keyed by edge.line; the DDG is keyed by\n     (symbol_id, variable, def_line)), and aliased-receiver reasoning IS section 7b-excluded.\n\nDURABILITY HAZARD to fix before either measurement is trusted: INV-busis's instruments\n(walk_anatomy2.py / walk_anatomy3.py) exist only under a previous session /tmp scratchpad, are not\nin the repo, and do not run against today's _ddg_taint_reaches signature (it grew twice — #203\nadded defs_at/inherits, #214 added barrier_lines). Re-pointing them and landing them in-repo is\nstep zero, and the extent of the drift is NOT DETERMINED."  # e4aa
    fields: {}  # e4aa
