  message: "EXIT CONDITION RATIFIED BY THE OWNER, 2026-08-06. Verbatim: \"straightened out\nmeans the human has good vibes. thats it. the human will tell you when its\nstraightened out. nothing further.\"\n\nTHIS ITEM'S \"NOT DECIDED\" IS NOW DECIDED. The decision is that there are NO\ncriteria. Not a checkable list, not a rubric, not a readiness assessment, not\na decision package to be judged against. The owner will say when. Update the\ndescription's \"WHAT THE OWNER HAS AND HAS NOT DECIDED\" accordingly: the\nopen question it names is closed.\n\nWHAT THIS FORBIDS, stated so no future session re-derives it:\n  - Do NOT draft an exit condition. Asked and answered.\n  - Do NOT ask the owner what \"straightened out\" means. \"Nothing further.\"\n  - Do NOT invent a gate, threshold, score, metric or pass/fail vector. That\n    was already the standing rule; it now extends to the softer forms too --\n    a \"checkable list for human judgment\" is also out.\n  - Do NOT build a decision package whose purpose is to argue the area is\n    done, or to prompt the owner for a verdict.\n  - Do NOT resolve this carrier because a session judges the area ready.\n    Inactivity is not discharge and neither is self-assessment. The owner\n    discharges it.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE: the deferral itself still holds, this carrier still\nholds INV-zogud out of ready via isbefore, and the four violated invariants\n(INV-lupav P0, INV-busis, INV-sadah, INV-karud) are still worth fixing on\ntheir own merits. The work continues; only the exit CRITERIA question is\nclosed. Keep the owner informed of what actually moved -- that is the input\nto the vibes, and it is the only input we control.\n\nPROCESS NOTE. This was asked five sessions after the plan's S1 was scoped to\ndraft it and never did. An exit-condition drafting workflow was launched and\nKILLED mid-run on receipt of this ruling rather than allowed to finish and\nbe filed as a superseded artifact."  # b104
