  message: "CAMPAIGN PLAN RECORDED 2026-08-24, owner-directed (\"devise a plan to extinguish\nall of these issues at their roots\"). This carrier is the natural home for the\npointer, since the plan IS the proposed path to the end of the deferral this\nitem holds.\n\nFull plan: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint_root_extinguish_plan_08242026.md\nCompressed operating frame: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/LIVE.md section 4.\n\nSHAPE: the 67 open items across taint/dataflow/ddg/io_boundary/verify_claims/\nadr_0017 (27 violated, 28 todo_hard, 5 P1) are ~SIX ROOT FAMILIES, each with a\nchokepoint fix -- or a dated declared blindness where capacity is deferred.\n\nORDER, with the rationale that fixes the order: P0 verify premises (statuses\nare demonstrably stale: INV-pirot filed 08-06 is likely closed by WI-sajis done\n08-24) -> P1 fail-open family (\"never looked\" must read UNKNOWN -- a lying\ninstrument corrupts every later measurement, so this precedes measuring) -> P2\nlabel vocabulary (INV-tutar: env_read->host_secret, 48/85 flows @22.9%, the\nlargest single quantified precision loss) -> P3 measurement 0005 re-baseline ->\nOWNER RE-RANKS -> P4 refutation capacity -> P5 gate correctness + the WI-lutuh\nstdlib campaign (rust 33 -> js 13 -> python 53) -> P6 recall class INV-linub,\nGATED on the P3 number per the standing band ruling -> P7 identity/label\nstragglers.\n\nEXIT: every family closed-with-evidence or declared-blind + 0005 published ->\nPROPOSE releasing this carrier so INV-zogud re-enters ready. The exit itself is\nthe owner's declaration (ruling on record: human vibes, no criteria) -- the\nchecklist is input, never self-certification.\n\nOWNER DECISION POINTS, explicit so none is decided alone: (1) P2 boundary/label\nsplit ratification; (2) P3->P6 re-rank; (3) P5 instrument decision for\njava/swift/objc/scala completeness; (4) exit.\n\nThis item stays todo_hard and keeps blocking INV-zogud throughout -- that is\nits job; nothing here works the carrier directly."  # cf01
- op: discuss  # 2971
  at: '2026-08-25T20:11:46Z'  # 2971
  by: agent  # 2971
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2971
  clock: 8  # 2971
  nonce: '2971'  # 2971
  message: "P3 IS DONE: measurement 0005 is published (docs/measurements/0005-taint-precision-after-vocabulary-split.md), census of 0004's five-repo cohort at ba01153095.\n\nHEADLINE, both units, per this item's campaign plan: 21.6% per SITUATION (8 TP of 37) and 10.0% per ROW (17 TP of 170). Per-situation is 2.16x per-row -- the third population in a row where the units differ by roughly that factor. Positive control printed first: 0 CONFIRMED verdicts on any of the five repos -- 13 violated, 22 inconclusive.\n\nTHE FINDING THAT REFRAMES THE NUMBER. 0004 reported 297 rows on this cohort; this run reports 170. That is NOT a precision fix. host_secret ships three claims (network/logging/host_fs); host_description, created by the INV-tutar split, deliberately ships ONE (network). Re-running the identical census with two scope-probe claims added restores 0004's population REPO FOR REPO -- caddy 219, mitmproxy 60, poetry 13, express 3, apollo-server 2, total 297 -- and the 170 rows are a strict subset by flow identity, with all 127 extras carrying a probe claim id. So on this cohort P1's fail-open fixes removed nothing (consistent with what they do: they turn false CLEANS into unknowns) and the whole reduction is one scope decision.\n\nMETHOD, AND THE PART THAT MATTERS MOST. The WI-sivuz pre-registered adversarial control was run on the owner's explicit authorisation. Four independent adjudicators, disjoint chunks, given the flow and the source but not the primary label: DISAGREEMENT RATE 0.0% over all 37, including both contested cases. AND THEN THE TWO PASSES THAT FOLLOWED CHANGED THE HEADLINE TWICE, IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS -- a commissioned adjudication overturned the one label the primary pass had flagged as contested (row 7.9% -> 10.6%), and an adversarial refuter broke 1 of the 9 true positives (situation 24.3% -> 21.6%, row 10.6% -> 10.0%). So 0001's caveat is not a formality: a zero disagreement rate shows the RUBRIC was applied consistently, not that it is right, because both passes share it. A blind pass alone would have published a number that was wrong in both directions at once.\n\nWHAT IS NOW OWED TO THE OWNER, and this item is where it lands: THE P3 RE-RANK. The band ruling (~41% => <50% => \"precision is the headline problem; RECALL WORK SHOULD STOP\") stands until the owner re-ranks on this number. Nothing in 0005 moves the band by itself -- the bands were named before any interval was computed, precisely so a later interval could not argue them down. P6 (the INV-linub recall class: WI-nasuf, WI-makij, INV-mumov L3, INV-gijis/tanom/suril, WI-nakut's java half) stays stopped until that re-rank.\n\nCAMPAIGN STATE: P0 done, P1 done (6 PRs), P2 done (owner-ratified), P3 done. Next unblocked work is P4 (capacity: INV-busis, WI-gotun, WI-tizig) and P5 (gate correctness then the stdlib campaign), neither of which is gated on the re-rank."  # 2971
