  message: "OWNER DECISION POINT 2, RE-RULED 2026-09-06. Verbatim: \"so put it on the\nrecord. phase 6 is unblocked.\"\n\nTHE NUMBER IT WAS RULED ON: measurement 0012\n(docs/measurements/0012-taint-precision-after-escape-closure.md, dev\nf247b52587, published 2026-09-02): useful precision 30.9% pooled (29/94\nsituations), 28.0% unweighted per-repo mean, against the standing band of\n<=25%. 0006 had read 24.1% and tripped it; the 2026-08-26 re-rank\n(p3_rerank_08262026.md) stopped Phase 6 on that reading. 0012's own text:\n\"The band does not trip on either estimator.\"\n\nWHAT CHANGES: the Phase 6 recall class -- INV-linub (class), INV-mumov L3,\nINV-gijis, INV-tanom, INV-suril, WI-nakut's java half; WI-nasuf and WI-makij\nalready done -- is no longer held by the band ruling. INV-linub at P1 is the\nhighest-priority open item and `ready` sorts by priority, so it rises to the\nhead mechanically.\n\nWHAT DID NOT CHANGE: the plan's method rule that every recall PR ships its\nMARGINAL PRECISION measurement and carries awaits_bakeoff_validation; the\nPhase 7 list; the exit, which stays the owner's declaration.\n\nRecorded here because the 2026-08-26 stop was recorded here and in the plan;\nmirrored on INV-linub and in taint_root_extinguish_plan_08242026.md decision\npoint 2 so no home still reads \"STAYS STOPPED\"."  # f2ce
- op: discuss  # 9f4a
