  nonce: 9f4a  # 9f4a
  message: "ARC-FINISHING ORDER, owner ruling 2026-09-06. Supersedes the tail of the\n2026-08-26 re-rank (\"Phase 5 -> Phase 7 -> recall\"); everything before that\ntail is closed.\n\n  WI-lunav + WI-zumoz -> INV-nular\n  -> Phase 5 residue: [javascript leg, if unfiled] -> WI-dupok -> WI-lavut\n  -> WI-gotun (java def/use extractor, or a dated declared blindness)\n  -> Phase 7: WI-jokij + WI-gudak -> INV-sadah -> INV-karud\n              -> INV-dulah lang-slot limb -> re-scope INV-kurup, INV-nanon\n  -> Phase 6 recall (unblocked 2026-09-06 on 0012):\n              INV-linub -> INV-mumov -> INV-gijis -> INV-tanom -> INV-suril\n              -> WI-nakut (java half)\n  -> INV-busis\n\nSTAGE NOTES\n1. WI-lunav, WI-zumoz: INV-nular's own second and third passes. They already\n   hold it out of `ready` via isbefore; no new edges.\n2. INV-nular: the catalogue kind-vs-semantics class. P1, unchanged.\n3. Phase 5 residue. Before WI-dupok, confirm whether the plan's javascript\n   leg (13 modules, rust -> js -> python) landed inside WI-lutuh (PR #573)\n   or was never filed; if never filed, file it and it precedes WI-dupok.\n   go (no toolchain) and java/objc/scala (premise unverified; instrument\n   decided 2026-08-26 on WI-lutuh) are NOT scheduled. File work items if\n   they should be; otherwise they remain plan prose and nothing waits on\n   them.\n4. WI-gotun before any java-side recall. java has no def/use extractor, so\n   every java flow is structural and the sanitizer arm can never credit a\n   java barrier. A java recall PR's marginal precision number would read\n   low for false positives a sanitizer would have cleared. Ship the\n   extractor or a dated declared blindness; silence stays banned.\n5. Phase 7. WI-jokij and WI-gudak together: one family (module slot vs the\n   `external` sentinel; swift is one of WI-jokij's five languages). Then\n   INV-sadah, INV-karud, INV-dulah's lang-slot limb, then re-scope the two\n   META items against whatever their populations have drained to.\n6. Phase 6 recall. INV-linub is the class item; an L3 fix under it is\n   measured through the taint path, not io-boundaries chain counts\n   (INV-linub, 2026-09-04). INV-mumov is already isbefore'd behind it.\n   Every recall PR ships its MARGINAL PRECISION measurement and carries\n   awaits_bakeoff_validation.\n7. INV-busis last. Capacity, not correctness: its 2026-09-02 entry limits\n   the escape-closing payoff to flows whose first walk already returned\n   True.\n\nCLOSED, NOT SCHEDULED: INV-zidur (the ddg_mixed label split), WI-kabif,\nINV-fumod, WI-nasuf, WI-makij. WI-tizig is wont_do.\n\nBINDING. `ready` sorts by priority and INV-linub is P1 against a P2\nPhase 7, so the queue would contradict this order. Encode it with isbefore\nedges, not re-ranks: --add-isbefore INV-linub on WI-dupok, WI-lavut,\nWI-gotun, WI-jokij, WI-gudak, INV-sadah, INV-karud, INV-dulah, INV-kurup,\nINV-nanon (10 edges; the carrier pattern), and --add-isbefore INV-busis on\nINV-linub (1 edge). Priorities stay what the items are worth. Every target\nis open, so the never-isbefore-onto-a-satisfied-item rule holds. Remove the\nedges as each stage closes; an edge whose source is resolved stops\nblocking on its own.\n\nEXIT: unchanged. Every family closed with behavioural evidence or converted\nto a dated, user-visible declared blindness; then PROPOSE releasing the\nWI-nazos carrier. The release itself is the owner's declaration."  # 9f4a
